numpy: Highway's vectorized sort, argsort and partition on wasm.

numpy's CPU dispatch has no wasm targets, so np.sort, np.argsort and
np.partition fell back to scalar code. Call Highway's VQSortStatic and
VQSelectStatic (WASM SIMD128 target) directly for 16-, 32- and 64-bit
keys. Highway's float select duplicated values when given infinities and
NaNs, so floats are selected as order-preserving integer keys. argsort is
a key-value sort of (key, index) pairs, for 32-bit keys and 64-bit
floats, the types where it beats the scalar argsort. NaNs sort last, as
in numpy. Highway's seed uses clock(), which WASI lacks, so use
clock_gettime there. Used by toolchain/recipes.toml.

